      "severity": "blocking-for-clean-accept",
      "axis": "f0_binding closure (all three classes)",
      "finding": "The landed rev13 repair resolves the pointer but does not close the chain. F1/F2a/F2b now declare consistency_evidence_sha256=9e335e9ba1bf and the live evidence measures 9e335e9ba1bf (pointer PASS), but that evidence document carries no map_taxonomy_sha256, no lead_contract_sha256 and no measured_at, so it cannot be tied to the declared F0 bytes 0abb9ed8a961 or the supplement d7419b4e8963. Execution controls: (a) the canonical tool is byte-deterministic on unchanged inputs (9e335e9b twice), so the pointer is durable but nominal; (b) mutating an unchecked F0 field changes the F0 hash while the tool output stays byte-identical -- the evidence hash is not a function of the F0 bytes; (c) mutating a compared field does change the output, so the gap is specifically the missing input-hash binding, not a blind checker. The rev27 closure item (e) regression reported by F1-review-090 F090-05, F2b-rev12-069 HF-069F2B-I09, F2a-review-19 HF-19-F2A-3, F2a-review-043 HF-043-2 and F2b-review-022 therefore survives the landed repair.",
